# Vantage

Per-deal AI agent for HubSpot. Monorepo at hackathon 1/vantage-hackathon.

## Structure
- `apps/web` — Next.js 15 App Router frontend (port 3000)
- `apps/api` — FastAPI backend (port 8000)
- `packages/mcp-server` — MCP tools for deal intelligence

## API client (do not break)
- All frontend API calls go through `apps/web/src/lib/api.ts`
- Keep `accountsApi`, `draftsApi`, `signalsApi` method signatures unchanged unless explicitly asked
- Dev auth: `NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_BYPASS_TOKEN` in `apps/web/.env.local` matches `DEBUG_BYPASS_TOKEN` in `apps/api/.env`

## UI design system
- Neutrals: `zinc-*` only (migrate any `gray-*` to `zinc-*`)
- Primary actions: `bg-zinc-900 text-white` — not indigo gradients
- No `Sparkles` icons for AI labels; use subtle text badges or nothing
- No `bg-gradient-to-*` hero banners; use white cards with left border accents
- Reuse classes from `apps/web/src/app/globals.css`: `.card`, `.section-header`, `.btn-accent`, urgency dots
- Font: Inter (already configured)

## Demo
- Demo account: `python scripts/seed_demo_account.py` in `apps/api` (Meridian Ops)
- Do NOT run agents on the 9 seeded showcase accounts — it replaces MEDDPICC state
- Remove or hide "Simulate" / "Sample" buttons — pre-seed data instead for demo trust
- Trigger agents: War Room "Run Agent" or `POST /v1/accounts/batch-refresh`

## Scope discipline
- One page per agent session when possible
- Extract components from large files instead of growing them
- No drive-by refactors outside the requested page